Here is a concise map of how teacher filtering works in `SmartCalendar.vue`. There is **no** ref named `selectedTeacher`; the closest equivalents are `filterTeacherId`, `weekViewTeacherId`, and `teacherSearch`, plus role-scoping via `currentTeacherId`.

---

## Teacher selection state (exact names)

| Name | Kind | Role |
|------|------|------|
| `teachers` | `ref([])` | Raw list from `GET /api/v1/teachers` (normalized). |
| `filterTeacherId` | `ref('')` | Narrows **courses** and **visible teacher columns** to one teacher; set from prop `initialTeacherId`, **not** from a toolbar control in the template. |
| `weekViewTeacherId` | `ref('')` | Which teacher the **週檢視** grid and chips use; synced with `initialTeacherId` when provided. |
| `teacherSearch` | `ref('')` | Text filter on teacher **names** for `visibleTeachers`. |
| `roomFilter` | `ref('')` | Filters `visibleTeachers` by room (affects which teacher columns/chips appear). |
| `studentSearch` | `ref('')` | Also constrains `visibleTeachers` (AND with matching courses). |
| `currentTeacherId` | `computed` | `String(props.userId)` when present; teacher role uses this to scope data. |
| `initialTeacherId` | `prop` | Parent-driven “jump to this teacher”; watcher copies into `filterTeacherId` + `weekViewTeacherId`. |

Supporting computeds: `filterTeacherOptions`, `visibleTeachers`, `weekOverviewActiveTeacher`, `filteredCourses`, `schedulerTeachers` (modal only).

```754:768:frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const props = defineProps({
  branchId: [String, Number],
  userRole: String,
  userId: [String, Number],
  initialTeacherId: [String, Number],
  resetWeekToken: [String, Number],
});
// ...
const isTeacher = computed(() => props.userRole === 'teacher');
const currentTeacherId = computed(() => {
  const raw = props.userId;
  if (raw == null || raw === '') return null;
  return String(raw);
});
```

